>> title: Cheddar Cheese Sauce
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: cheese, milk, roux, vegetarian, stovetop
>> counters: Diner, Meat and Three
>> aka: cheese sauce, mornay sauce
>> servings: 6
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: narrow — cheddar boiled in a sauce splits into oil and rubbery strings, so it goes in off the heat and only off the heat
>> step.1: melt
>> step.2: cook roux 1 min
>> step.3: whisk in, simmer 5 min
>> step.4: melt in off heat

Melt @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(40 g) in a #heavy saucepan{} over medium heat.

Cook @all-purpose flour{3%Tbs}(25 g) in @&(~1)butter{} for ~{1%min}, whisking.

Whisk @whole milk{2%cups}(475 mL; warmed) into @&(~1)roux{} a splash at a time and simmer for ~{5%min}, until it coats a spoon.

Melt @sharp cheddar{8%oz}(225 g; coarsely grated), @Dijon mustard{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, @cayenne{1/8%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/4%tsp} into @&(~1)white sauce{} off the heat.
